    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for postgresql16-pgvector.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 10.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Open-source vector similarity search for Postgres. Supports L2 distance, inner product, and cosine distance\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* pgvector: pgvector: Arbitrary code execution via out-of-bounds write during IVFFlat index build (CVE-2026-103484)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
